<article class="env-lemma" id="0B3K">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B3K">Lemma <span data-tag="0B3K">30.11.5</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a regular scheme. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\mathcal{F}$ is Cohen-Macaulay and $\text{Supp}(\mathcal{F}) = X$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{F}$ is finite locally free of rank $> 0$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $x \in X$. If (2) holds, then $\mathcal{F}_ x$ is a free $\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$-module of rank $> 0$. Hence $\text{depth}(\mathcal{F}_ x) = \dim (\mathcal{O}_{X, x})$ because a regular local ring is Cohen-Macaulay (Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00NQ" data-tag="00NQ">10.106.3</a>). Conversely, if (1) holds, then $\mathcal{F}_ x$ is a maximal Cohen-Macaulay module over $\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$ (Algebra, Definition <a href="/tag/00NF" data-tag="00NF">10.103.8</a>). Hence $\mathcal{F}_ x$ is free by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00NT" data-tag="00NT">10.106.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>